-- title:
--   Rank q closed subscheme generated by a q-torsion section
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring and let $\mathcal G$ be a family of relative group laws assigning, to every commutative $A$-algebra $T$ and every projective Weierstrass curve over $T$ with unit discriminant, a group law on the functor of sections of the morphism `projModelStrCR` from the Proj of the graded quotient ring to $\operatorname{Spec} T$. Assume $\mathcal G$ is chord-and-tangent, i.e. for every such pair there is a bijection between sections over a field and the affine point group of the base change which is additive and compatible with Galois twists, and that $\mathcal G$ is origin-normalised, i.e. for every such pair the identity section is cut out by a ring homomorphism $\chi$ from the origin chart ring killing both $x/y$ and $z/y$. Let $q$ be prime, let $T$ be a local $A$-algebra, let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $T$ with $\Delta_W$ a unit, and let $P$ be a section of `projModelStrCR W.toProjective` over $\mathrm{id}_{\operatorname{Spec} T}$ such that the $q$-fold iterate of the group law applied to $P$ is the identity section, and such that for no ring homomorphism $\chi$ from the origin chart ring to $T$ does $P$ reduce to the origin, meaning $P$ is the $\chi$-origin-chart section with both $\operatorname{originParam}\chi$ and $\operatorname{originW}\chi$ in the maximal ideal. Then there exist a scheme $K$ and a closed immersion $\iota : K \to \operatorname{Proj}$ such that $\iota$ followed by the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} T$ is finite, flat and locally of finite presentation with rank $q$ at every point; every multiple $[i]P$ ($i \in \mathbb N$) factors through $\iota$; two morphisms out of the Proj agreeing after composition with all $[i]P$ agree after composition with $\iota$; and for every closed immersion $j : Z \to \operatorname{Proj}$ through which all $[i]P$ factor, $\iota$ factors through $j$.
--
--   This constructs the constant subgroup scheme of order $q$ generated by a $q$-torsion section with non-trivial reduction — over a local base the multiples $[i]P$, $0 \le i < q$, have pairwise distinct reductions, so their disjoint union is a finite flat closed subscheme of rank $q$ — and characterises it by the two universal properties that make it the scheme-theoretic union of those sections (the group structure on $K$ is not asserted). It feeds into [`WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.exists_isClosedImmersion_finrank_eq_comp_eq_comp_one_of_comp_eq_schemeNsmul_of_nsmul_eq_one`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.exists_isClosedImmersion_finrank_eq_comp_eq_comp_one_of_comp_eq_schemeNsmul_of_nsmul_eq_one), in the treatment of level structures on Weierstrass curves.
